    {
      "@id": "urn:nabou:att_dfaa7846c8e5a8696a22d063",
      "@type": "Attestation",
      "schema:name": "Astypalaia was an excellent hideout for corsairs, not only because they could find provisions there (such as bread, wine, etc.) and stock up with drinking water, but also because the island provided plenty of safe anchorages.",
      "properties": {
        "status": "UNREVIEWED",
        "historically_verified": false
      },
      "historically_verified": false
    },
    {
      "@id": "urn:nabou:cite_2cfc817e03c48d68b9b3be02",
      "@type": "Citation",
      "schema:name": "{\"end_char\": 2441, \"end_line\": 31, \"original_inspected\": false, \"pdf_file\": \"library_acquisition/18f781280144b88f0b78dfa5.pdf\", \"printed_page\": null, \"scan_indexes_0_based\": [0, 1], \"source_file\": \"18f781280144b88f0b78dfa5.txt\", \"start_char\": 161, \"start_line\": 7, \"url\": \"https://hdl.handle.net/10442/18865\"}",
      "properties": {
        "source_id": "src_8fb3b0a89051d4c69fbc8d7dc79dbc33",
        "locator": "{\"end_char\": 2441, \"end_line\": 31, \"original_inspected\": false, \"pdf_file\": \"library_acquisition/18f781280144b88f0b78dfa5.pdf\", \"printed_page\": null, \"scan_indexes_0_based\": [0, 1], \"source_file\": \"18f781280144b88f0b78dfa5.txt\", \"start_char\": 161, \"start_line\": 7, \"url\": \"https://hdl.handle.net/10442/18865\"}",
        "exact_excerpt": "\nAt the same time, Astypalaia was an excellent hideout for corsairs, not only because they could ﬁnd provi-\nsions there (such as bread, wine, etc.) and stock up with drinking water, but also because the island provided\nplenty of safe anchorages.",
        "attribution": "stated"
      },
      "historically_verified": false
    },
    {
      "@id": "urn:nabou:att_7b488d46ad443c0e37e061e7",
      "@type": "Attestation",
      "schema:name": "The names of Astypalaia’s havens in French and Italian portolan texts, along with other information of the time (testimonies about corsair contracts written on the island and marriages between privateers and local Greek women), attest not only the strong relationship that the corsairs built with Astypalaia, but also the degree of appropriation of the place by them.",
      "properties": {
        "status": "UNREVIEWED",
        "historically_verified": false
      },
      "historically_verified": false
    },
    {
      "@id": "urn:nabou:cite_ff305ab2e755c9acbc0c6bb1",
      "@type": "Citation",
      "schema:name": "{\"end_char\": 2441, \"end_line\": 31, \"original_inspected\": false, \"pdf_file\": \"library_acquisition/18f781280144b88f0b78dfa5.pdf\", \"printed_page\": null, \"scan_indexes_0_based\": [0, 1], \"source_file\": \"18f781280144b88f0b78dfa5.txt\", \"start_char\": 161, \"start_line\": 7, \"url\": \"https://hdl.handle.net/10442/18865\"}",
      "properties": {
        "source_id": "src_8fb3b0a89051d4c69fbc8d7dc79dbc33",
        "locator": "{\"end_char\": 2441, \"end_line\": 31, \"original_inspected\": false, \"pdf_file\": \"library_acquisition/18f781280144b88f0b78dfa5.pdf\", \"printed_page\": null, \"scan_indexes_0_based\": [0, 1], \"source_file\": \"18f781280144b88f0b78dfa5.txt\", \"start_char\": 161, \"start_line\": 7, \"url\": \"https://hdl.handle.net/10442/18865\"}",
        "exact_excerpt": " The names of Astypalaia’s havens in French and Italian portolan texts, along with\nother information of the time (testimonies about corsair contracts written on the island and marriages\nbetween privateers and local Greek women), attest not only the strong relationship that the corsairs built\nwith Astypalaia, but also the degree of appropriation of the place by them.",
        "attribution": "stated"
      },
      "historically_verified": false
    },
    {
      "@id": "urn:nabou:att_60dc40fc124a5081886bec3b",
      "@type": "Attestation",
      "schema:name": "The consulted source reports that Stathis Romanos Manetas utilized Phournoi as a base and secure anchorage during his operations in the Chios area in 1694 and 1695, which remains a conjecture.",
      "properties": {
        "status": "UNREVIEWED",
        "historically_verified": false
      },
      "historically_verified": false
    },
    {
      "@id": "urn:nabou:cite_cb8edf1dd235f30113957484",
      "@type": "Citation",
      "schema:name": "{\"end_char\": 1175743, \"end_line\": 13979, \"original_inspected\": false, \"pdf_file\": \"library_acquisition/bad2f54f36da12ea92871556.pdf\", \"printed_page\": null, \"scan_indexes_0_based\": [336], \"source_file\": \"bad2f54f36da12ea92871556.txt\", \"start_char\": 1174278, \"start_line\": 13966, \"url\": \"https://nepub.lib.uoa.gr/index.php/aura/article/view/2979\"}",
      "properties": {
        "source_id": "src_e1b01396ea1212c71904bf8747e7bb74",
        "locator": "{\"end_char\": 1175743, \"end_line\": 13979, \"original_inspected\": false, \"pdf_file\": \"library_acquisition/bad2f54f36da12ea92871556.pdf\", \"printed_page\": null, \"scan_indexes_0_based\": [336], \"source_file\": \"bad2f54f36da12ea92871556.txt\", \"start_char\": 1174278, \"start_line\": 13966, \"url\": \"https://nepub.lib.uoa.gr/index.php/aura/article/view/2979\"}",
        "exact_excerpt": " Nonetheless, whether Stathis Romanos Manetas utilized Phournoi as a base and secure an-\nchorage during his operations in the Chios area in 1694 and 1695 remains a conjecture.",
        "attribution": "stated"
      },
      "historically_verified": false
    },
    {
      "@id": "urn:nabou:att_51df0caec95b30f59d16c1f2",
      "@type": "Attestation",
      "schema:name": "The consulted source reports that the British governor constructed a fort on New Providence in 1695 and named it Nassau in honor of King William III.",
      "properties": {
        "status": "UNREVIEWED",
        "historically_verified": false
      },
      "historically_verified": false
    },
    {
      "@id": "urn:nabou:cite_be3e615ef1793776cb6bf370",
      "@type": "Citation",
      "schema:name": "{\"end_char\": 12300, \"end_line\": 802, \"original_inspected\": false, \"pdf_file\": null, \"printed_page\": null, \"scan_indexes_0_based\": [], \"source_file\": \"6616b6c9e3e3e375c17fbbc2.txt\", \"start_char\": 10475, \"start_line\": 801, \"url\": \"https://doi.org/10.2307/1007328\"}",
